{#
  SONiC BGP, container deployment.

  The VM template (bgp/sonic.j2) opens with a "no router bgp" reset. docker-sonic-vs starts with no
  BGP process at all, and vtysh rejects that line with rc 13 ("Failure to communicate[13] to bgpd,
  line: no router bgp" / "% No BGP process is configured").

  Under SONiC's INTEGRATED vtysh config that error is fatal to the run: vtysh abandons the file and
  exits 13, so netlab reports "bgp configuration ... failed" -- while still having applied the rest
  of it, so BGP ends up correctly configured and netlab reports failure anyway. A retry then
  succeeds, because a BGP process exists by then, which disguises the whole thing as a startup race.

  There is no render-time-safe form of the reset: "no router bgp <as>" fails identically on a node
  that has never had a BGP process. Emitting none matches bgp/frr.j2, which emits none either.

  The cost, accepted deliberately: a redeploy no longer clears stale BGP state, so a neighbor
  removed from the topology survives until "netlab down".

  Before the device was parented to FRR the container had no bgp template of its own and fell
  through to bgp/frr.j2. This file keeps that behaviour now that bgp/sonic.j2 would otherwise be
  selected by the <device>.j2 lookup.
#}
{% include "frr.j2" +%}
